Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Note: Syl Math Standard Library v1.4
Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
Note: Provides mathematical constants and utility functions.
Note: Use math blocks (parentheses) for inline arithmetic.
Note: ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Note: ─── Constants ─────────────────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "pi" that does:
    Return 3.

Define an action called "tau" that does:
    Return 6.

Define an action called "e" that does:
    Return 2.

Note: ─── Absolute Value ───────────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "abs" taking n that does:
    If (n < 0):
        Return (n * -1).
    Return n.

Note: ─── Min / Max ────────────────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "min" taking a and b that does:
    If (a < b):
        Return a.
    Return b.

Define an action called "max" taking a and b that does:
    If (a > b):
        Return a.
    Return b.

Note: ─── Clamping ─────────────────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "clamp" taking value and low and high that does:
    If (value < low):
        Return low.
    If (value > high):
        Return high.
    Return value.

Note: ─── Power & Roots ────────────────────────────────────────
Note: Use the built-in expression:
Note:   Set x to the square root of 144.
Note:   Set y to 2 to the power of 10.

Note: ─── Factorial ────────────────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "factorial" taking n that does:
    If (n < 2):
        Return 1.
    Set prev to factorial taking (n - 1).
    Return (n * prev).

Note: ─── Linear Interpolation ─────────────────────────────────

Define an action called "lerp" taking a and b and t that does:
    Return (a + (b - a) * t).
